FCEUmm (https://github.com/libretro/libretro-fceumm, GNU General Public License version 2) runs the NES, and like every
libretro core it says nothing of the instructions it runs. The tools apply this change of Dreamports' own to its source
before building it on the contributor's computer (tools/consoles.mjs, tools/libretro/build.mjs), so the program that
plays the original (tools/libretro/host.c) can ask to be told of each one: its address, where that is in the
cartridge's program whatever bank is switched in there, its first byte, and the processor's registers. That's how the
code map learns which functions ran in play, and gameplay proven which instructions and which way each branch went
(tools/lib/played.mjs).

The processor only calls the function it was given, when it was given one, between reading an instruction and running
it: nothing of the console changes, so every frame's picture and sound are the same with it or without, which
tools/test/real-console.mjs checks. Nothing of FCEUmm is in the repository but the lines of its own this change sits between.

diff --git a/src/drivers/libretro/libretro.c b/src/drivers/libretro/libretro.c
index 55cf607..9dd860a 100644
--- a/src/drivers/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/src/drivers/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -3392,6 +3392,25 @@ static void retro_run_blit(uint8_t *gfx)
 #endif
 }
 
+/* Dreamports: the processor tells the tools' program of every instruction (x6502.c), with where its address is in the
+ * cartridge's program, as an offset from its first byte, whatever bank is switched in there, or 0xFFFFFFFF outside
+ * it, as in the console's memory. retro_dreamports_ran gives the function to tell, or none. Its name starts as
+ * libretro's own do, as those are the only names this core lets out (link.T). */
+extern void (*DreamportsRan)(uint32_t pc, uint32_t op, uint32_t axys, uint32_t p);
+static void (*dreamports_told)(uint32_t pc, uint32_t place, uint32_t op, uint32_t axys, uint32_t p);
+
+static void dreamports_ran(uint32_t pc, uint32_t op, uint32_t axys, uint32_t p)
+{
+   uintptr_t at = (uintptr_t)Page[pc >> 11] + pc - (uintptr_t)PRGptr[0];
+   dreamports_told(pc, PRGptr[0] && Page[pc >> 11] && at < PRGsize[0] ? (uint32_t)at : 0xFFFFFFFF, op, axys, p);
+}
+
+RETRO_API void retro_dreamports_ran(void (*told)(uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t))
+{
+   dreamports_told = told;
+   DreamportsRan   = told ? dreamports_ran : NULL;
+}
+
 void retro_run(void)
 {
    uint8_t *gfx;
